ave uncovered the burial site of Sekhentyu-Ptah in the Saqqara necropolis, marking a significant find in ancient Egyptian history. With inscriptions indicating his prominent roles, the site boasts a funerary chapel and sealed sarcophagi, alongside complex burial shafts and a variety of artifacts. These elements suggest a sprawling burial network, and ongoing explorations will further illuminate the history of burial practices in this ancient site.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/egyptian-archaeologists-uncovered-a-tomb-at-saqqara-with-3-sealed-sarcophagi-and-more-than-100-figurines-from-later-burials/articleshow/134304573.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/egyptian-archaeologists-uncovered-a-tomb-at-saqqara-with-3-sealed-sarcophagi-and-more-than-100-figurines-from-later-burials/articleshow/134304573.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-17T14:10:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134304645,imgsize-132059.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Dwayne Johnson: "Be humble. Be hungry. And always be…"]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134305278.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-dwayne-johnson-be-humble-be-hungry-and-always-be-a-powerful-lesson-in-staying-grounded-after-success/articleshow/134305278.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-dwayne-johnson-be-humble-be-hungry-and-always-be-a-powerful-lesson-in-staying-grounded-after-success/articleshow/134305278.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-17T16:10:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134305448,imgsize-28242.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New York City volunteers planted 20,000 marsh seedlings in 2003; 80% were healthy by 2005]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134306485.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[New York City's Big Egg Marsh restoration began with planting 20,000 cordgrass seedlings.  Volunteers and scientists worked to re-establish the salt marsh ecosystem.  Despite early challenges, vegetation successfully covered over eighty percent of the site.  This successful project paved the way for further marsh restoration efforts.  Jamaica Bay has since seen over 150 acres of marshland restored.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-york-city-volunteers-planted-20000-marsh-seedlings-on-a-dying-salt-marsh-in-2003-but-80-of-the-site-was-healthy-just-two-years-later/articleshow/134306485.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-york-city-volunteers-planted-20000-marsh-seedlings-on-a-dying-salt-marsh-in-2003-but-80-of-the-site-was-healthy-just-two-years-later/articleshow/134306485.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-17T18:15:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134306598,imgsize-1461406.cms"/></item></channel></rss>